                <pb facs="0193" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.512H11/422: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-10T13:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10,
                                1919—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:52 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Your instruction number 882, October 29. Secretary of State Desvernine says
                    [he is] giving serious study to problem with desire [to] meet the wishes [of the
                    Department,] but asks explanation of the oral statement as indicated in [the]
                    last ten lines of instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
